PrayerFragment.onViewCreated — smali edits (classes_classes6/.../PrayerFragment.smali)
=======================================================================================

Two edits:

(1) Bump the register count of onViewCreated so we have scratch registers v5..v7:

    .method public onViewCreated(Landroid/view/View;Landroid/os/Bundle;)V
-       .locals 5
+       .locals 8

(2) Insert the spread block immediately AFTER the left reader's openFile call and
    BEFORE the ".line 158" marker. At that point the registers hold:
        p2 = left PDFView      p1 = pdf asset path (String)
        v0 = pages (ArrayList) v1 = start page (int)   v2 = scrollY (int)

    ...
        invoke-virtual {p2, p1, v0, v1, v2}, Lorg/chabad/kehossiddur/PDFView;->openFile(Ljava/lang/String;Ljava/util/ArrayList;II)Lru/mobigroup/bookreader/MuPDFCore;
+
+       # === TABLET TWO-COLUMN SPREAD (added) ===
+       invoke-virtual {p2}, Landroid/view/View;->getParent()Landroid/view/ViewParent;
+       move-result-object v5
+       instance-of v6, v5, Landroid/view/ViewGroup;
+       if-eqz v6, :spread_skip
+       check-cast v5, Landroid/view/ViewGroup;
+       invoke-virtual {v5}, Landroid/view/ViewGroup;->getChildCount()I
+       move-result v6
+       const/4 v7, 0x2
+       if-lt v6, v7, :spread_skip
+       const/4 v7, 0x1
+       invoke-virtual {v5, v7}, Landroid/view/ViewGroup;->getChildAt(I)Landroid/view/View;
+       move-result-object v5
+       instance-of v6, v5, Lorg/chabad/kehossiddur/PDFView;
+       if-eqz v6, :spread_skip
+       check-cast v5, Lorg/chabad/kehossiddur/PDFView;
+       add-int/lit8 v6, v1, 0x1
+       invoke-virtual {v5, p1, v0, v6, v2}, Lorg/chabad/kehossiddur/PDFView;->openFile(Ljava/lang/String;Ljava/util/ArrayList;II)Lru/mobigroup/bookreader/MuPDFCore;
+       invoke-virtual {v5}, Lorg/chabad/kehossiddur/PDFView;->checkHasSizes()V
+       :spread_skip
+       # === END TABLET TWO-COLUMN SPREAD ===

        .line 158
    ...

Why it's safe on phones: layout/prayer_fragment.xml makes the reader's sibling the alert
include (a LinearLayout), so getChildAt(1) is not a PDFView and the instance-of check skips.
On tablets, layout-sw600dp/prayer_fragment.xml makes child 1 the second PDFView.
